Priya Nair: Verified perf runs on dedicated staging. Throughput improvement looks solid; please document canary rollout plan in release notes.
Maya Chen: Approved after small nits; LGTM.
// wavefront_hyperfusion.cu - inner tile loop
for (int t = 0; t < TILE_T; ++t) {
  // load Q,K,V fragment into registers
  load_qkv_fragment(q_frag, k_frag, v_frag, base_ptr);
  // apply rotary in-register
  apply_rotary_inplace(q_frag, t);
  // fused qk multiply + softmax reduction
  fused_qk_softmax_accumulate(q_frag, k_frag, acc);
}
// write KV-fragments ready for async conductor
write_kv_fragment(dst_kv, acc);
// async_kv_conductor.cc - prefetch hint
void Conductor::OnRequest(const RequestMeta& r) {
  if (can_prefetch(r)) schedule_prefetch(r.prefix_hash);
}
// wavefront_policy.cc - micro-batching trigger
if (queued_tokens >= policy.min_tokens_for_wavefront) {
  emit_wavefront_batch();
} else {
  fallback_to_continuous_batch();
}
Microbench (seq=128, bs=1): p50 latency -19% (from 42.7ms -> 34.8ms), throughput +38%
Microbench (seq=64, mixed batch): p99 tail -12%
Continuous-batching replay (10k requests, mixed seq 16/64/512): end-to-end cost per token -14% on dedicated pool
KV stall time reduction: median stall -48% when conductor enabled
Memory traffic: global DRAM reads reduced ~26% in hot paths
Introduce Wavefront Hyperfusion attention kernel and async-KV conductor. Improves latency and throughput for mixed-length continuous batching. Feature gated; canary rollout planned.

Context and motivation: Several customers and internal benchmarks showed inconsistent latency and throughput for long-context models when rotary and rope positional encodings were mixed across model families. The runtime was selecting a generic FlashAttention variant that did not account for rope compensation or token-importance for KV cache eviction, which led to suboptimal batching and premature KV spills under load. This PR introduces the FlashAdaptive adapter: a small compatibility layer + kernel selection glue that enables a fused rotary/rope compensation path, integrates a priority-aware KV eviction policy, and exposes scheduling hints to continuous-batcher so the runtime can pick the optimal kernel variant based on sequence distribution and quantization profile. What this PR does (single-string summary): Adds flash_adaptive kernel adapter and fused rope/rotary compensator, implements KV Priority Evict manager (recency + token-weight heuristic), hooks into continuous-batcher for policy-driven kernel routing, includes micro-benchmarks and integration tests, and ships a docs page with guidance and rollout feature-flag. Commits (high-level): - 7a1d2f: introduce flash_adaptive adapter interface and selection table; - 9c3b8e: implement fused_rope_rotary_compensator (CUDA + C++ wrapper) with numerics safeguards; - b2f9d1: kv/cache_priority_manager: implement eviction scoring and async prefetch hooks; - d4e7c3: continuous_batcher: expose scheduling hints and add policy binding for flash_adaptive; - 3f22a0: tests: add perf harnesses and unit tests for eviction heuristics; - 0b5c7f: docs: add docs/perf/flashadaptive.md and rollout checklist.
--- a/runtimes/attn/flash_adaptive/adapter.cu
+++ b/runtimes/attn/flash_adaptive/adapter.cu
@@ -1,3 +1,12 @@
+// small shim to pick optimized kernel based on seq_len, qk_dtype, and rope_presence
+if (seq_len > 1024 && uses_rope) {
+  launch_fused_rope_rotary_kernel(...);
+} else {
+  launch_flash_default(...);
+}

--- a/runtimes/kv/cache_priority_manager.cpp
+++ b/runtimes/kv/cache_priority_manager.cpp
@@ -20,6 +20,22 @@
+double score = recency_weight * recency_score + token_weight * token_importance;
+if (score < eviction_threshold) {
+  schedule_eviction(key);
+}
+// async prefetch hint to batcher for likely next prefix
+emit_prefetch_hint(request_id, predicted_prefix_id);

Representative numbers from internal perf harness: seq=512 (bs=16) P50 latency -5% and throughput +8%; seq=2048 (bs=8) throughput +12-18% depending on quantization; memory peak reduced ~6% due to fewer KV spills when eviction policy enabled. Numbers measured with feature-flag on vs off, averaged across 5 runs.
