Motivation: Interactive workloads with bursty short requests were experiencing tail latency spikes caused by repeated KV cache/decoder thrashing when many small prefill windows overlapped with decode work. This PR introduces a slab-based admission controller and epoched prefill windows to reduce mid-pipeline contention and stabilize kernel scheduling. Design summary: 1) Slab admission: classify incoming prefill candidates into size-classes (tiny, small, medium, large) and admit them into per-slab token reservoirs. Admission enforces configurable concurrency caps per slab so tiny bursts cannot evict medium/large prefills on the same GPU worker. 2) Epoched prefill windows: prefill requests are grouped into short epochs (configurable, default 8ms). Within an epoch we coalesce KV priming and schedule a single warm-pass kernel for compatible size-classes to improve KV cache locality. 3) Kernel coordinator: a thin adaptive coordinator chooses between doing a coalesced warm kernel across an epoch or allowing immediate decode handoff based on real-time metrics (KV hit rate, outstanding decode backlog, per-slab occupancy). 4) Soft backpressure and gentle requeue: when slabs are saturated we apply a lightweight backpressure token to upstream batching; requests are either requeued into the next epoch or opportunistically forwarded to a lower-cost model variant. Implementation notes: - Scheduler changes in runtime/scheduler/slab_admission.cc (approx 680 LOC added/modified). - New metrics in observability/metrics/prefill_slabs.{yaml,proto}. - Config knobs exposed via config/runtime.yaml: slab_sizes, epoch_ms, slab_caps, epoch_coalesce_threshold. - Unit/integration tests under tests/scheduler/test_slab_admission.py and tests/e2e/prefill_epoch_coalescing.py. Performance results (internal perf lab, p50/p99 latencies vs main): - p50 generation latency: -3.2% (better by reduced jitter) - p95 generation latency: -7.9% - p99 token latency: -12.4% for bursty short-prefill workloads - KV cache warmup hit rate improved from 62% to 83% for mixed-size traces Rollout plan: feature-gated behind runtime.prefill_slab_admission; staged rollout to canary fleet (10%) -> 50% -> 100% with automatic rollback on p99 regressions >10%. Checklist: [x] design doc linked [x] unit tests [x] integration tests [x] perf numbers attached [x] config toggles + conservative defaults [x] metrics and dashboards updated
